  "description_short": "Hidden gem at the Crags serving hearty breakfasts and honest comfort food in a relaxed garden setting.",
  "description_long": "Tucked away in the Mill Decor Centre along Animal Alley in the Crags, Peppermill Cafe is one of those places locals keep coming back to. The relaxed garden atmosphere makes it easy to linger over a proper breakfast or a leisurely lunch, with plenty of shade and a genuinely welcoming vibe.\n\nThe menu focuses on comfort classics done right—think generous breakfasts, fresh salads, and satisfying mains that don't try to be fancy. It's the kind of food that just works, whether you're stopping in after exploring nearby Monkeyland and Birds of Eden, or you're a regular who knows exactly what you're ordering. The outdoor seating makes it ideal for families and anyone with a dog in tow.\n\nConveniently located between Plettenberg Bay and Nature's Valley, it's a solid midway stop that feels more like a neighbourhood secret than a tourist spot. Fair prices, consistent quality, and that easygoing Garden Route hospitality that keeps people talking.",
